a magic -1 number. What do you think of this approach ?\r\n\r\nI'm a bit worried whether anyone relys on the specific address value. Before if a virtual method is invalid its address is `nullptr`, if we use -1 it will be `0xFFFFFFFF`, both are clearly invalid values. But if we use a dummy variable the address will be a random and seemingly normal value. If someone dereference the pointer the error message will be confusing. There's little chance anyone will use it like this though, but better check if there are any black magic in use.","created_at":"2025-04-02T11:33:39Z","updated_at":"2025-04-02T11:33:39Z","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104264#discussion_r2024640236","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/104264","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2024640236"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104264#discussion_r2024640236"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/104264"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2024640236/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":34,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":2021040005,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":23,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2025037300","pull_request_review_id":2736631838,"id":2025037300,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOAO6SJc54s530","diff_hunk":"@@ -30,10 +29,12 @@\n \t\t\t\t_gdvirtual_##$VARNAME = (void *)_get_extension()->get_virtual2(_get_extension()->class_userdata, &_gdvirtual_##$VARNAME##_sn, hash);\\\\\n \t\t\t}\\\\\n \t\t\t_GDVIRTUAL_GET_DEPRECATED(_gdvirtual_##$VARNAME, _gdvirtual_##$VARNAME##_sn, $COMPAT)\\\\\n-\t\t\t_GDVIRTUAL_TRACK(_gdvirtual_##$VARNAME, _gdvirtual_##$VARNAME##_initialized);\\\\\n-\t\t\t_gdvirtual_##$VARNAME##_initialized = true;\\\\\n+\t\t\t_GDVIRTUAL_TRACK(_gdvirtual_##$VARNAME);\\\\\n+\t\t\tif (_gdvirtual_##$VARNAME == nullptr) {\\\\\n+\t\t\t\t_gdvirtual_##$VARNAME = reinterpret_cast<void*>(static_cast<uintptr_t>(-1));\\\\","path":"core/object/make_virtuals.py","commit_id":"057858a0fb703b7f314fe3fbff85a1abda92595d","original_commit_id":"5e5b27142d0ed107b582a92592d42c832e3e6362","user":{"login":"dsnopek","id":191561,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5MTU2MQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/191561?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek","html_url":"https://github.com/dsnopek","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"If we use an actual address, it should probably be the address of a function, so if something attempts to call it, it will at least work in a minimal sense and try to give a nice message.\r\n\r\nSo, we could have:\r\n\r\n```\r\nvoid _invalid_gdextension_virtual_function() {\r\n  CRASH_NOW_MSG(\"Attempting to call invalid GDExtension virtual function.\");\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\n... and then use `&_invalid_gdextension_virtual_function` as our sentinel value representing \"invalid\"\r\n\r\nI don't know how that affects doing stuff at compile time, though","created_at":"2025-04-02T15:03:50Z","updated_at":"2025-04-02T15:04:09Z","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104264#discussion_r2025037300","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/104264","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2025037300"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104264#discussion_r2025037300"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/104264"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2025037300/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":34,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":2021040005,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":23,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2027115624","pull_request_review_id":2740065215,"id":2027115624,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOAO6SJc5401Ro","diff_hunk":"@@ -30,10 +29,12 @@\n \t\t\t\t_gdvirtual_##$VARNAME = (void *)_get_extension()->get_virtual2(_get_extension()->class_userdata, &_gdvirtual_##$VARNAME##_sn, hash);\\\\\n \t\t\t}\\\\\n \t\t\t_GDVIRTUAL_GET_DEPRECATED(_gdvirtual_##$VARNAME, _gdvirtual_##$VARNAME##_sn, $COMPAT)\\\\\n-\t\t\t_GDVIRTUAL_TRACK(_gdvirtual_##$VARNAME, _gdvirtual_##$VARNAME##_initialized);\\\\\n-\t\t\t_gdvirtual_##$VARNAME##_initialized = true;\\\\\n+\t\t\t_GDVIRTUAL_TRACK(_gdvirtual_##$VARNAME);\\\\\n+\t\t\tif (_gdvirtual_##$VARNAME == nullptr) {\\\\\n+\t\t\t\t_gdvirtual_##$VARNAME = reinterpret_cast<void*>(static_cast<uintptr_t>(-1));\\\\","path":"core/object/make_virtuals.py","commit_id":"057858a0fb703b7f314fe3fbff85a1abda92595d","original_commit_id":"5e5b27142d0ed107b582a92592d42c832e3e6362","user":{"login":"MarianoGnu","id":1776044,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NzYwNDQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1776044?v=4","gravatar_id":""